.TH SKYDSECD 8 "2026-08-08" "Skydio" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
skydsecd \- Skydio security compliance reporting daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skydsecd
.RB [ \-d ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-V ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skydsecd
reports whether required Skydio security tooling is present on the host,
along with identifying information about the host itself.
.PP
It listens on TCP port 2014 on all interfaces.  On each accepted
connection it probes the host and writes four newline-separated fields to
the client, then closes the connection:
.IP 1. 4
the hostname, as reported by
.BR gethostname (2);
.IP 2. 4
the baseboard serial number read from
.IR /sys/class/dmi/id/board_serial ,
or an explanation of why it could not be read;
.IP 3. 4
whether the WS1 hub utility is installed and executable;
.IP 4. 4
the current date and time.
.PP
The host is probed once per connection rather than once at startup, so
tooling installed or removed while the daemon is running is reflected in
the next reply without a restart.
.PP
No request is read from the client.  Connecting is the entire protocol.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Write diagnostic tracing to standard error.  Without this option,
failures to read host information are reported only in the reply sent to
the client.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreground
Do not fork into the background.  Required when running under a service
manager that supervises the process directly, which is why the shipped
systemd unit passes it.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/dmi/id/board_serial
Read to obtain the baseboard serial number.  On a stock system this file
is mode 0400 and owned by root, so
.B skydsecd
must run as root to read it; otherwise the serial is reported as
unreadable.  If the file is owned by uid or gid 65534 the daemon
concludes it is running in an unprivileged container and does not attempt
the read.  If the file is present but empty, the host is reported as
likely being a virtual machine.
.TP
.I /opt/vmware/ws1\-hub/bin/ws1HubUtil
Checked for existence and execute permission.
.TP
.I /etc/default/skydsecd
.TQ
.I /etc/sysconfig/skydsecd
Optional environment files read by the systemd unit, if present.
.SH SECURITY
.B skydsecd
performs no authentication and applies no access control.  Any host able
to reach port 2014 can retrieve the hostname and hardware serial number.
Restrict access at the network layer.
.PP
The daemon is linked statically so that it does not resolve its
dependencies through shared objects on the host whose integrity it is
reporting on.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits non-zero if the listening socket cannot be created, bound or
listened on.  Once serving, errors affecting a single connection are
logged under
.B \-d
and do not terminate the daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR skydsec (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Alvin Cura <alvin.cura@skydio.com>
